# Provenance and license for patterns.graphml

Upstream:   https://github.com/BeksOmega/pattern-language-graph
Commit:     1404507682a027e02cab4ecf6edf16d771f826e1
Retrieved:  2026-07-18
SHA-256:    f107192313d9a68f0a9dfc24eddec3a595c82da20da0a2af54203cd1a4c8a939
Contents:   253 nodes, 1858 directed edges. Node attrs: label, name, section,
            subsection, stars. Edge attr: origin (start|end).

The file encodes factual metadata about Christopher Alexander, Sara Ishikawa,
and Murray Silverstein, "A Pattern Language" (Oxford University Press, 1977):
pattern numbers, names, confidence asterisks, section groupings, and the
cross-reference structure. It contains none of the book's prose.

scripts/convert-graphml.ts refuses any file whose SHA-256 does not match the
hash pinned above; re-vendoring is a deliberate step that updates this file.

Corrections to the data are made in the conversion script (precondition-keyed),
never by editing patterns.graphml. See the corrections list in
scripts/convert-graphml.ts and data-notes/validation.md.

